.TH GIT-MUTATE 1 "October 2026" "git-mutate" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-mutate \- break the code on purpose and report whether the tests noticed
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git handles
.B \-\-help
before invoking external subcommands, so the complete help is provided by the command's
.B \-h
option instead:
.PP
.RS
.B git mutate \-h
.RE
.PP
That help includes the mutations-file format, a worked example, the guards, and the exit statuses.
.SH SHELL CHECKS
Use
.B \-\-env lines
for a check that is a script, not a test runner. Other ecosystems are
pytest (the default), mvn, go, rust, and dotnet.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail-pattern " regex"
Required with lines. Each matching output line is one failure, classified as an
assertion kill by default. Patterns are Python regular expressions searched after
ANSI colors are stripped.
.TP
.BI \-\-error-pattern " regex"
Optional, lines only. Recognizes error kills, including lines that do not match
the failure pattern. If both patterns match, the error classification wins unless
overridden by the assertion pattern.
.TP
.BI \-\-assertion-pattern " regex"
Marks a matching failure message as an assertion kill, including when the error
pattern matched. It does not recognize new failure lines by itself.
.PP
The named groups
.B id
and
.B msg
provide the failure id and message. Each absent or unmatched group uses the whole
line instead. Groups come from the failure pattern when it matches, otherwise
from the error pattern. Stable ids allow already failing checks to be excluded
by the baseline.
.PP
A nonzero exit with no matching line is not measured. A zero exit with no matches
is green; executed checks cannot be counted. The fast tier turns itself off,
even with an explicit fast command. Runner compilation heuristics do not apply.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.nf
git mutate \-\-env lines \-\-fail-pattern '^FAIL: ' \\
  \-\-cmd 'sh scripts/check_clean_install.sh' mutations.toml
.fi
.RE
.PP
For structured messages, use a pattern such as
.BR "^FAIL: (?P<id>[^:]+): (?P<msg>.*)$" .
Per-project defaults in .git/info/git-mutate accept
.B fail_pattern
and
.BR error_pattern .
